# g95-fu-takeover-feed desktop wiring (the core half is native/core/crates/pending-wire/g95-fu-takeover-feed.wire)

1. preload/host-api.ts (hot): delete the two members
       provideSecretInput: (requestId, value) => invokeIpc(DESKTOP_IPC.provideSecretInput, requestId, value),
       takeoverReady: (sessionId, id) => invokeIpc(DESKTOP_IPC.takeoverReady, sessionId, id),
   (line ~190). desktop-api-split.ts now lists both in DIRECT_KEYS.secrets (composed by renderer/core-direct/api-takeover.ts over the
   window's core connection), so `DesktopHostApi` no longer has them: until this edit `tsc -p tsconfig.node.json` fails at host-api.ts:190-191.
   Then main/ipc-sessions.ts (~240-245) loses the two `handle(DESKTOP_IPC.provideSecretInput ...)` / `handle(DESKTOP_IPC.takeoverReady ...)`
   handlers and shared/contract-ipc.ts the two DESKTOP_IPC keys (nothing calls them any more).

2. The mirrors, for SINGLETONS-DELETE (main/takeover-gate.ts `createTakeoverMirror`, main/secret-requests.ts `createSecretSlotMirror`, both
   fed by the core's `takeover/state` once the rows of g95-fu-takeover-feed.rows are applied and packages/protocol is regenerated):
   a TakeoverStateReader is `(ids) => coreClient.call('takeover/state', ids?.length ? { secretRequestIds: ids } : {})`. In main/index.ts build
   it once beside `takeoverGate` (line ~1126) and pass `createTakeoverMirror(read)` where `takeoverGate.assertFree` is read (browser/host-agent.ts
   `host.assertFree`, which becomes async) and `createSecretSlotMirror(read).has` where `secretInputs.has` is read. The gate's own drain,
   expiry and ready() (takeoverGate.onSessionState/onExpire/ready, takeover-feed.ts, takeover-state.ts) are then the deletion of
   SINGLETONS-DELETE: the core owns them (CoreTakeover::begin/ready, the card's own `expires_after`).

3. src/shared/desktop-api-split.test.mjs (companion of desktop-api-split.ts, not owned by this task), test
   'the direct half has the eight groups and sections holds only the key sections': the direct half now has nine groups.
   Replace its title with 'the direct half has the nine groups and sections holds only the key sections' and its two lines
       assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(DIRECT_KEYS), ['sessions', 'files', 'scm', 'terminal', 'settings', 'connections', 'capabilities', 'sections']);
       assert.equal(Object.values(DIRECT_KEYS).flat().length, 234);
   with
       assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(DIRECT_KEYS), ['sessions', 'files', 'scm', 'terminal', 'secrets', 'settings', 'connections', 'capabilities', 'sections']);
       assert.equal(Object.values(DIRECT_KEYS).flat().length, 236);
   (until then that test fails; src/preload/host-api.test.mjs keys_match_classification fails until step 1 is applied).
